<%#
  Atiman Report — capability denial page (ATM-002-I2E).

  Rendered when the canonical ATM-003 capability middleware refuses
  `finding.report`. It states the decision plainly and reveals no asset, no
  product state and no authority detail. No role or userRole appears here: the
  decision is a capability decision, and the page says so in the operator's terms.
%>
<div class="atiman-stack">
  <section class="atiman-card" aria-labelledby="report-denied-heading">
    <h2 class="atiman-card__title" id="report-denied-heading">Reporting is not available for your account</h2>
    <p class="atiman-note">
      Your account does not currently hold the authority to record observations.
      Nothing has been recorded and nothing has been changed.
    </p>
    <p class="atiman-card__note">
      If you believe you should be able to report observations against your
      organization's assets, ask an administrator to review your account's
      capabilities.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="atiman-card" aria-labelledby="report-denied-next-heading">
    <h2 class="atiman-card__title" id="report-denied-next-heading">Where you can go</h2>
    <div class="atiman-stack">
      <a class="atiman-action" href="/today">
        <span><span class="atiman-action__label">Today</span></span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
      </a>
      <a class="atiman-action" href="/atiman/asset">
        <span>
          <span class="atiman-action__label">Look up an asset</span>
          <span class="atiman-action__hint">Identity and operating context only</span>
        </span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
